  <h1>Boiler Advice for Acomb Homeowners</h1>
  <p>Acomb is where we're actually based, so if you're reading this from an Acomb postcode, we're probably a five-minute drive away right now. That means faster response on emergencies, and it means we know this patch better than most. Here's what we get asked most often by Acomb homeowners — costs, how to check who you're letting into your house, and what to do when the boiler stops playing ball.</p>

  <h2>How much does a new boiler cost in Acomb?</h2>
  <p>A like-for-like combi swap starts from £2,000, and a system-to-combi conversion (where the pipework needs more work) starts from £3,000. Most Acomb jobs come in somewhere between £2,000 and £3,000 — the exact figure depends on the boiler you choose and what's already in the house. We always quote in writing, for free, before anything's agreed.</p>
  <p>See our <a href="/new-boiler-installation-acomb/">New Boiler Installation in Acomb</a> page for pricing specifics, or our <a href="/advice-centre/new-boiler-cost/">full cost breakdown guide</a> and <a href="/advice-centre/combi-vs-system-boiler/">combi vs system comparison</a> if you're still weighing up which type of boiler you actually need.</p>

  <h2>Finding a Gas Safe engineer in Acomb</h2>
  <p>Anyone working on your boiler in Acomb — or anywhere — should be Gas Safe registered, and you can check their number on the official register before they set foot inside. We're registered under 570248, Worcester Bosch and Ideal accredited, and we've been trading in plumbing and heating for 18 years, first as Acomb Plumbing &amp; Heating, now as The Boiler Doctor. A fair few calls we get start with someone who's been let down by a previous engineer — if that's you, it's a genuinely easy thing to put right.</p>

  <h2>Boiler breakdowns — what to do first</h2>
  <p>No heating or hot water is the most common call we get, and it's often a pressure, valve, or PCB fault that we can diagnose and fix in a single visit. Check your pressure gauge first — below 1 bar usually means a leak or a recent radiator bleed. If there's an error code on the display, tell us what it says when you call; it often tells us most of what we need before we've even left the van.</p>
  <p>If you're calling about an elderly parent, a poorly relative, or a house with a new baby in it, let us know — those go straight to the top of the list, no messing about.</p>
  <p>Our <a href="/boiler-repairs-acomb/">Boiler Repairs &amp; Breakdowns in Acomb</a> page has our current call-out pricing, and being based here means we're often able to get to Acomb jobs the same day.</p>

  <h2>Don't wait for it to break — get it serviced</h2>
  <p>An annual service is £100 + VAT and keeps your manufacturer's warranty valid — most people don't find that out until it's too late. Landlords in Acomb, this is also where your CP12 gas safety certificate comes from; see our <a href="/gas-safety-landlords/">Gas Safety &amp; Landlords</a> page for what's legally required.</p>
  <p>If you'd rather not think about it, our <a href="/boiler-care-plans/">Boiler Care Plans</a> start from £12.99/month, include your annual service, and a free CO alarm.</p>

  <h2>Book an Acomb visit</h2>
  <p>New boiler quote, a repair, or your annual service — we're on your doorstep. Call and tell us what's happening; we'll give you a straight answer, not a script.</p>
